-- title:
--   Crossing model over a DVR has Krull dimension at least 2
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring that is a domain, a discrete valuation ring, and complete with respect to the adic filtration of its maximal ideal; let $\pi \in W$ be an irreducible element and let $E$ be a natural number with $1 \le E$. Form the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$, i.e. $W[[U,V]]$ with the two variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\ 2$, and let `uvCrossingIdeal` be the principal ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - \pi^{E}$, where $\pi^{E}$ is viewed as a constant power series. The assertion is that the quotient `UVCrossingModel W (π ^ E)`, that is $W[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi^{E})$, has Krull dimension at least $2$, the inequality being taken in $\mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$ with a bottom element adjoined, the value group of `ringKrullDim`. Only the lower bound is asserted; the matching upper bound is a separate statement.
--
--   This is the lower half of the computation that the local crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^{E})$, the standard form of the completed local ring of a curve at an ordinary double point over a discrete valuation ring, has Krull dimension exactly $2$. It is used in the analysis of stalks of models of modular curves at such points, for instance in [`AlgebraicCurve.isNoetherianRing_stalk_and_two_le_ringKrullDim_and_exists_eq_mul_pow_of_isPullback_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.isNoetherianRing_stalk_and_two_le_ringKrullDim_and_exists_eq_mul_pow_of_isPullback_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk) and in the proof that those stalks are integrally closed.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_two_le_ringKrullDim.lean

import Mathlib
